## TRUST-REGION METHODS

The most widely used trust-region methods for nonlinear equations simply apply Algorithm 4.1 from Chapter 4 to the merit function $f ( x )=\frac{1}{2} \| r ( x )\|_{2}^{2},$ using $B_{k}=J \left(x_{k}\right)^{T} J \left(x_{k}\right)$ as the approximate Hessian in the model function $m_{k} ( p )$ , which is defined as follows:

$$
m _ {k} (p) = \frac {1}{2} \| r _ {k} + J _ {k} p \| _ {2} ^ {2} = f _ {k} + p ^ {T} J _ {k} ^ {T} r _ {k} + \frac {1}{2} p ^ {T} J _ {k} ^ {T} J _ {k} p _ {k}.
$$
